    {
      "id": 206787,
      "name": "Meemitone",
      "username": "Meemitone",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/df788c/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-10-23T22:09:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>https://i.imgur.com/lRo7vXa.jpg is the current Agent of Chaos Logo, which I suspect is the art in question. On another note, I've realised that decks with more than 20 arts are required to have at least one unique card ,in fact they must have (X-20)*2 unique cards, where X is the number of arts for that deck (and that's given that all the other arts appear exactly twice each). Given that \"New hero character cards\" is it's own post-it, you can likely say they aren't included in the deck counts, so it looks like Benchmark has at least&nbsp;<strong>12</strong> unique cards! (of course, that includes the assumption that there's only 40 cards in his deck...)</p>",
      "post_number": 17,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:36:20.140Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
