      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Ok so, if there are only cards of which there are 1 or 2 copies, then there must be exactly 12 unique cards and 14 duoque cards (12*1 &amp; 14*2).\n\nIf there&#39;s the option of 3 copies of a card then here&#39;s a table:\n\nW is number of unique cards, X is number of duoque cards and Z is the number of trioque cards.\n\nW |X | Y\n\n13|12|1\n\n14|10|2\n\n15|08|3\n\n16|06|4\n\n17|04|5\n\n18|02|6\n\n19|00|7\n\nAdding in the possibility of 4 of a kind (a quartique, if you will) means generating multiple tables, one for each value of Z, the number of quartiques:\n\nZ=1\n\nW |X | Y\n\n15|09|0\n\n16|07|1\n\n17|05|2\n\n18|03|3\n\n19|01|4\n\nZ=2\n\nW |X | Y\n\n16|08|0\n\n17|06|1\n\n18|04|2\n\n19|02|3\n\n20|00|4\n\nZ=3\n\nW |X | Y\n\n18|05|0\n\n19|03|1\n\n20|01|2\n\nZ=4\n\nW |X | Y\n\n20|02|0\n\n21|00|1\n\n(If Z&gt;5 X or Y must be negative to compensate and you can&#39;t ship negative cards)\n\nBoy this was more work than I should&#39;ve given it  :stuck_out_tongue: \n\nEDIT: Oh hey it was all for naught, the count includes some character cards so the actual count comes down to&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">9 unique, 10 duos, 1 trio and 2 quartets from here:&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color: rgb(230, 236, 240); color: rgb(20, 23, 26); font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">https://twitter.com/GTGChristopher/status/922610361353809920</span>",
